                        "sense_id": "4241f592-5e3e-38a3-b540-acd3d123ca7d",
                        "entry_id": "6cf39c0f-a971-39ec-aa01-e071029a6b19",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who lights fires with petrol, especially (historical) a revolutionary who attacked public buildings in this way in Paris in 1871."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a4ecdbc7-a376-48f9-bdad-5a42a55524ce",
                                "sense_id": "4241f592-5e3e-38a3-b540-acd3d123ca7d",
                                "text": "Caution was necessary in moving about, the pavement had to be avoided, as the impression conveyed to the mind of the sentry, if he saw anyone near a house, was that it must be a petroleur or a petroleuse."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8c947d4f-89f5-4170-9159-a4eb8c25631a",
                                "sense_id": "4241f592-5e3e-38a3-b540-acd3d123ca7d",
                                "text": "1877, quoted in 1990, Walter Boehlich, The Letters of Sigmund Freud to Eduard Silberstein, 1871-1881#\nIn times like these one is tempted to turn into a petroleur."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4e759d62-af74-4b75-8b27-daab90fb395a",
                                "sense_id": "4241f592-5e3e-38a3-b540-acd3d123ca7d",
                                "text": "The work of the incendiaries of 1792 was only to be finished by the petroleurs of 1871. Night was come. A great number of the Parisian population were groaning, but the revolutionists triumphed with joy."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
